  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "Pre-K to postgrad, and everyone keeping it running.",
  "long_description": "Every room it happens in: the alphabet over a chalkboard with the lesson going on to it, a bench with the burner lit and two flasks working, and the four seconds at the end when the caps go up. A mortarboard on your picture with a tassel that swings, twenty-four crayons laid round it points inward, or slate in an oak frame with the chalk on the ledge. A banner and a trophy that carry the year you finished — you say which, and it offers this one. Then eight to wear, from the blocks to the diploma — an apple, alphabet blocks, the bus, a pencil, a burner, the diploma, the cap, and the year you finished.",
